% The Ponens policies agentic-ai-runtime-governance, as a program of Logical English for LPS.
%
% Written by lpsPlus's ponens_twin.pl (docs/migration/ponens.md) from 21
% Ponens policies, whose files are in sources/ (Ponens: github.com/imandra-ai/
% ponens, MIT licence), with 14 Ponens traces as its scenarios.
%
% Each step of a trace is an action of the session Ponens recorded. Each
% policy is a causal law that records a breach: at the step where the policy
% fails, when the step ends, or at the end of the session when the policy
% looks forward. Where a scenario has a comment above it, the comment is what
% Ponens's own evaluator (`ponens trace check --json`) says of the same
% policies on that trace.
%
% DISCLAIMER. This program was written by a translator from the policies of
% another system. It is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind,
% express or implied, including any warranty that it is accurate, complete or
% fit for a particular purpose. The translation may be wrong: check it against
% its source before relying on it. It is not legal, regulatory or other
% professional advice. Its authors accept no liability for any loss or damage
% arising from its use.

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 18.

the events are:
    step *a step* is a *a kind*; known as step_is_a.
    step *a step* shows *a sign*; known as step_shows.
    step *a step* comes after step *an other step* in its chain; known as chain_link.
    step *a step* comes after step *an other step* on its target; known as target_link.
    step *a step* ends; known as step_ends.
    the trace shows *a sign*; known as trace_shows.
    item *an item* of *a collection* has *a value* as *a field*; known as item_field.
    artifact *an artifact* is made by step *a step*; known as made_by_event.
    step *a step* uses artifact *an artifact*; known as uses_event.
    artifact *an artifact* is a *a kind* artifact; known as artifact_kind_event.
    artifact *an artifact* derives from artifact *an other artifact*; known as derives_event.
    the session ends; known as session_ends.

the fluents are:
    step *a step* was a *a kind*; known as was_a.
    step *a step* has shown *a sign*; known as has_shown.
    step *a step* is in the chain of step *an other step*; known as in_chain.
    step *a step* shares a target with step *an other step*; known as shares_target.
    step *a step* has ended; known as has_ended.
    the trace has shown *a sign*; known as trace_has_shown.
    item *an item* of *a collection* had *a value* as *a field*; known as item_had.
    artifact *an artifact* was made by step *a step*; known as made_by.
    step *a step* used artifact *an artifact*; known as used.
    artifact *an artifact* was a *a kind* artifact; known as artifact_kind.
    artifact *an artifact* derived from artifact *an other artifact*; known as derived.
    step *a step* meets *a condition*; known as meets.
    the trace meets *a condition*; known as trace_meets.
    the policy *a policy* is broken at step *a step*; known as broken_at.
    the policy *a policy* is broken; known as broken.

the knowledge base agentic ai runtime governance includes:

% What a trace records, kept to the end of the session.
when step a step is a a kind
then step the step was a the kind.

when step a step shows a sign
then step the step has shown the sign.

when step a step comes after step an other step in its chain
then step the other step is in the chain of step the step.

when step a step comes after step an other step on its target
then step the other step shares a target with step the step.

when step a step ends
then step the step has ended.

when the trace shows a sign
then the trace has shown the sign.

when item an item of a collection has a value as a field
then item the item of the collection had the value as the field.

when artifact an artifact is made by step a step
then artifact the artifact was made by step the step.

when step a step uses artifact an artifact
then step the step used artifact the artifact.

when artifact an artifact is a a kind artifact
then artifact the artifact was a the kind artifact.

when artifact an artifact derives from artifact an other artifact
then artifact the artifact derived from artifact the other artifact.

% agent_identity_resolved (error): G(action → agent_id_resolved ∧ kya_valid)
% FIX Gap 1 / Identity & Authorisation. A Red condition: an action by an agent whose identity cannot be resolved to a verified human principal is an authorisation failure requiring containment.
step a step meets "shows agent id resolved and shows kya valid" at a time if
    step the step has shown "agent id resolved" at the time
    and step the step has shown "kya valid" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "action"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "shows agent id resolved and shows kya valid"
then the policy agent_identity_resolved is broken at step the step.

% consequential_action_approved (error): G(Release ∨ Deploy → P(UserApproval ∧ authenticated))
% Capability gate: the approval gate must have been passed with an authenticated record before the consequential action. Conversational or implicit approval does not satisfy it.
step a step meets "is a Release or is a Deploy" at a time if
    step the step was a Release at the time.

step a step meets "is a Release or is a Deploy" at a time if
    step the step was a Deploy at the time.

step a step meets "an earlier step is a UserApproval and shows authenticated" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step was a UserApproval at the time
    and step the second step has shown "authenticated" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step meets "is a Release or is a Deploy"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step is a UserApproval and shows authenticated"
then the policy consequential_action_approved is broken at step the step.

% credential_not_expiring (warning): G(action → ¬credential_expiring)
% Amber / flag-refer: a soft identity condition. Execution may continue in restricted mode pending credential renewal.
when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "action"
    and step the step has shown "credential expiring"
then the policy credential_not_expiring is broken at step the step.

% dce_current_for_consequential (error): G(ToolCall ∨ Release ∨ Deploy → dce_current)
% A DCE is invalidated by any material change to model version, prompt class, or inference configuration; acting under an invalidated DCE is a Red containment event.
step a step meets "is a ToolCall or is a Release" at a time if
    step the step was a ToolCall at the time.

step a step meets "is a ToolCall or is a Release" at a time if
    step the step was a Release at the time.

step a step meets "is a ToolCall or is a Release or is a Deploy" at a time if
    step the step meets "is a ToolCall or is a Release" at the time.

step a step meets "is a ToolCall or is a Release or is a Deploy" at a time if
    step the step was a Deploy at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step meets "is a ToolCall or is a Release or is a Deploy"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "dce current"
then the policy dce_current_for_consequential is broken at step the step.

% decision_path_reconstructable (warning): G(Release ∨ Deploy → decision_path_present)
% Amber / flag: a DecisionPathID populated but not yet fully attributed is a soft condition — continue, but the decision graph must be reconstructable for audit.
step a step meets "is a Release or is a Deploy (2)" at a time if
    step the step was a Release at the time.

step a step meets "is a Release or is a Deploy (2)" at a time if
    step the step was a Deploy at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step meets "is a Release or is a Deploy (2)"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "decision path present"
then the policy decision_path_reconstructable is broken at step the step.

% default_deny_confirmed (error): G(ToolCall → P(default_deny_confirmed))
% Tier 4 capability control: default-deny-not-confirmed is a Red halt. Continuous authorisation must be established before the agent may invoke tools.
step a step meets "an earlier step shows default deny confirmed" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "default deny confirmed" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a ToolCall
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows default deny confirmed"
then the policy default_deny_confirmed is broken at step the step.

% dual_approval_critical (error): G(Release → P(UserApproval ∧ approver_1) ∧ P(UserApproval ∧ approver_2))
% Tier 4 default-deny governance: dual approval must be logged before a Critical Autonomous release. Distinctness of the two approvers is guaranteed by the governance layer.
step a step meets "an earlier step is a UserApproval and shows approver 1" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step was a UserApproval at the time
    and step the second step has shown "approver 1" at the time.

step a step meets "an earlier step is a UserApproval and shows approver 2" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step was a UserApproval at the time
    and step the second step has shown "approver 2" at the time.

step a step meets "an earlier step is a UserApproval and shows approver 1 and an earlier step is a UserApproval and shows approver 2" at a time if
    step the step meets "an earlier step is a UserApproval and shows approver 1" at the time
    and step the step meets "an earlier step is a UserApproval and shows approver 2" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a Release
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step is a UserApproval and shows approver 1 and an earlier step is a UserApproval and shows approver 2"
then the policy dual_approval_critical is broken at step the step.

% execution_linked_to_intent (error): G(ToolCall ∨ Release ∨ Deploy → intent_resolved)
% FIX Gap 2. Without an IntentID the execution cannot be linked back to the governance-layer decision that initiated it; minimum required for regulatory decision-chain reconstruction.
step a step meets "is a ToolCall or is a Release (2)" at a time if
    step the step was a ToolCall at the time.

step a step meets "is a ToolCall or is a Release (2)" at a time if
    step the step was a Release at the time.

step a step meets "is a ToolCall or is a Release or is a Deploy (2)" at a time if
    step the step meets "is a ToolCall or is a Release (2)" at the time.

step a step meets "is a ToolCall or is a Release or is a Deploy (2)" at a time if
    step the step was a Deploy at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step meets "is a ToolCall or is a Release or is a Deploy (2)"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "intent resolved"
then the policy execution_linked_to_intent is broken at step the step.

% legal_entity_vlei_present (error): G(action → vlei_present)
% FIX Identity domain. GLEIF vLEI binds the legal entity at transaction time; absence is a Red hard-identity failure.
when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "action"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "vlei present"
then the policy legal_entity_vlei_present is broken at step the step.

% no_guard_violation (error): G(¬guard_violation)
% Szpruch trajectory conformance: a logged guard violation (e.g. Lmax guard, policy-boundary breach) is a Red halt requiring human resolution.
when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "guard violation"
then the policy no_guard_violation is broken at step the step.

% no_prohibited_transition (error): G(¬prohibited_transition)
% Szpruch governed transition system: a prohibited-transition attempt is the highest-priority Red halt after a hard identity failure — block, log the attempt, require root-cause analysis before restart.
when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "prohibited transition"
then the policy no_prohibited_transition is broken at step the step.

% no_release_without_authenticated_approval (error): G(Release ∨ Deploy → P(UserApproval ∧ authenticated ∧ approval_scope_covers))
% FIX Approval & Release Gating + Szpruch C4. Release with conversational or implicit approval, or approval whose scope does not cover the action, is a Red halt.
step a step meets "is a Release or is a Deploy (3)" at a time if
    step the step was a Release at the time.

step a step meets "is a Release or is a Deploy (3)" at a time if
    step the step was a Deploy at the time.

step a step meets "an earlier step is a UserApproval and shows authenticated and shows approval scope covers" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step was a UserApproval at the time
    and step the second step has shown "authenticated" at the time
    and step the second step has shown "approval scope covers" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step meets "is a Release or is a Deploy (3)"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step is a UserApproval and shows authenticated and shows approval scope covers"
then the policy no_release_without_authenticated_approval is broken at step the step.

% numeric_recomputed_deterministically (error): G(Compute → deterministic_recompute)
% Szpruch C2 failure mode: silent numeric error with LLM plausibility masking the arithmetic error. Ratios and thresholds must be recomputed deterministically.
when step a step ends
    and step the step was a Compute
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "deterministic recompute"
then the policy numeric_recomputed_deterministically is broken at step the step.

% outputs_policy_constrained (error): G(Draft → template_compliant)
% Szpruch C3 failure mode: approval-gate reasoning-around or prohibited language in output. Drafting must produce outputs compliant with approved templates, not free-form generation.
when step a step ends
    and step the step was a Draft
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "template compliant"
then the policy outputs_policy_constrained is broken at step the step.

% policy_reference_current (error): G(action → policy_current)
% Acting under a superseded or revoked policy is a Red failure; PolicyRefID is the FIX analogue of a certified policy reference.
when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "action"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "policy current"
then the policy policy_reference_current is broken at step the step.

% retrieved_data_attributed (error): G(Retrieve → provenance_checked ∧ recency_checked)
% Szpruch C1 failure mode: stale data used without flagging, or prompt injection via a retrieved document. The fix is enforceable attribution, not model self-report.
step a step meets "shows provenance checked and shows recency checked" at a time if
    step the step has shown "provenance checked" at the time
    and step the step has shown "recency checked" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a Retrieve
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "shows provenance checked and shows recency checked"
then the policy retrieved_data_attributed is broken at step the step.

% telemetry_spans_complete (error): ∀ s ∈ telemetry . s.status = recorded
% FIX Gap 3 / DecisionPathID substrate. Telemetry that is absent or cannot be reconstructed is a Red halt: the execution trajectory cannot be audited.
the trace meets "some item of telemetry fails the trace: ∀ s ∈ telemetry . s.status = recorded" at a time if
    item an item of telemetry had a value as a field at the time
    and it is not the case that item the item of telemetry had "recorded" as status at the time.

the trace meets "the trace: ∀ s ∈ telemetry . s.status = recorded" at a time if
    it is not the case that the trace meets "some item of telemetry fails the trace: ∀ s ∈ telemetry . s.status = recorded" at the time.

when the session ends
    and it is not the case that the trace meets "the trace: ∀ s ∈ telemetry . s.status = recorded"
then the policy telemetry_spans_complete is broken.

% tool_call_budget (warning): count(ToolCall) ≤ 20
% Amber / flag: approaching the tool-call budget is a near-miss that should notify human oversight and increment the session-level escalation counter, short of a halt.
the trace meets "the number of steps that is a ToolCall is at most 20" at a time if
    a number is the count of each S such that
        step S has ended at the time
        and step S was a ToolCall at the time
    and the number =< 20.

when the session ends
    and it is not the case that the trace meets "the number of steps that is a ToolCall is at most 20"
then the policy tool_call_budget is broken.

% tool_calls_allowlisted (error): G(ToolCall → in_allowlist)
% Szpruch capability control: a tool call outside all approved lists is a Red halt. Tier 2 governance enforces the allowlist as policy-as-code, not prompt guidance.
when step a step ends
    and step the step was a ToolCall
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "in allowlist"
then the policy tool_calls_allowlisted is broken at step the step.

% trajectory_within_bound (error): count(action) ≤ 50
% Szpruch maximum-trajectory-length guard. Exceeding Lmax indicates a runaway or looping workflow and is a Red halt; the bound is part of the certified DCE.
the trace meets "the number of steps that shows action is at most 50" at a time if
    a number is the count of each S such that
        step S has ended at the time
        and step S has shown "action" at the time
    and the number =< 50.

when the session ends
    and it is not the case that the trace meets "the number of steps that shows action is at most 50"
then the policy trajectory_within_bound is broken.

% within_constraint_scope (error): G(action → within_constraint_scope)
% FIX Intent & Constraint. An action outside the certified constraint scope is a Red hard failure; the ConstraintSet enables post-trade verification that execution was within declared scope.
when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "action"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "within constraint scope"
then the policy within_constraint_scope is broken at step the step.

